mapping "V8930.1" source="V8930" target="36198007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V8930 = Swedish national extension of V89.3 (Person injured in unspecified
        nonmotor-vehicle accident, traffic) with activity suffix SNOMED CT 36198007. Base V89.3 has Athena
        edges to SNOMED CT 444074 (Victim of vehicular AND/OR traffic accident, code 36198007) and 4168046
        (Vehicle accident, 418161006). Target 444074 is the most specific traffic-accident victim
        concept. Activity suffix (sport/work/etc.) is administrative context OMOP records on the
        visit/episode, not the diagnosis, so the standard injury target is identical across activity
        variants; the map drops the activity detail (broader). Confidence : Athena crosswalk on the base
        code, but source is unspecified-vehicle and activity context is lost.
        """
}
mapping "V8931.1" source="V8931" target="36198007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V8931 = Swedish extension of V89.3 with activity suffix SNOMED CT 36198007. Same reasoning
        as V8930: base V89.3 SNOMED CT 444074 (Victim of vehicular AND/OR traffic accident) and 4168046.
        444074 selected as the most specific traffic-accident victim target. Activity suffix carries no
        clinical-distinction in the injury target; broader.
        """
}
